# Copy to .env and adjust. SQLite keeps the zero-config local story:
#   bun run db:push && bun run db:seed

# ---- Database -------------------------------------------------------------
# SQLite by default (zero-config local dev). The `db/` folder lives at the
# repo root (git-ignored, recreated by db:push + db:seed). A RELATIVE
# `file:` URL is resolved against prisma/schema.prisma — exactly like the
# Prisma CLI — so `file:../db/custom.db` points at <repo>/db/custom.db for
# the CLI (migrate/seed), `next build`, and the running server alike,
# regardless of the process working directory. The runtime resolution rule
# lives in prisma/db-url.ts and is used by src/lib/db.ts + prisma/seed.ts
# (every PrismaClient goes through resolveDatabaseUrl()).
# For production, an ABSOLUTE path is still recommended — see
# docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §4.
# To use PostgreSQL:
#   1. Set provider = "postgresql" in prisma/schema.prisma
#   2. Set DATABASE_URL to a PostgreSQL connection string
#   3. bun run db:push && bun run db:seed
DATABASE_URL="file:../db/custom.db"
# PostgreSQL example:
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/nexuslearn

# ---- Site ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Canonical public origin — used for metadata, sitemap.xml, and robots.txt.
# Set to the deployed URL in production.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Session signing secret for HMAC cookie auth.
# REQUIRED in production: generate with `openssl rand -hex 32`.
# Falls back to an insecure dev-only constant when unset.
AUTH_SECRET=""
